From 7557aa05720896ac84d3fbeb0b5bd6f3883033d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:29:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] media: qcom: camss: vfe: don't delete a VFE
 power-domain link twice

vfe_pm_domain_off() calls device_link_del() on vfe->genpd_link even
when the link is already gone (a repeated or failed power-down), which
dereferences NULL (seen on MSM8996 when stopping a stream after the
pipeline had failed to power up once).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i64chehV1XxwjxyaGp
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index 319d19158..45acb1a4a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -878,7 +878,8 @@ void vfe_isr_reset_ack(struct vfe_device *vfe)
  */
 void vfe_pm_domain_off(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 {
-	if (!vfe->genpd)
+	/* the link is gone after a failed or repeated power-down */
+	if (!vfe->genpd || !vfe->genpd_link)
 		return;
 
 	device_link_del(vfe->genpd_link);
-- 
2.56.0

